From 15de6180b680351a7ca014905760db5e656aa02a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:42:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/75] perf(msm): AVX-512 IFMA batch-affine drain for native
 Stage 6a

Runtime-dispatched (x86-64 only, __builtin_cpu_supports avx512f+ifma; BB_MSM_NO_IFMA
disables). The tree reduce queues pairs limb-major in a per-thread buffer; the drain runs
8 Montgomery prefix chains in the lanes of 5x52-bit IFMA registers (R = 2^256, i.e. bb's
Montgomery domain: four 52-bit steps plus one 48-bit step), one scalar inversion of the 8
chain products, and the backward pass finishes each affine add. Outputs are fully reduced.
Drains of <= 6 pairs run the scalar formulas on the same queue.

Same pairing and same sums, so MSM results and proofs are unchanged.
